## 3. Entry Points & API Layer

### [app/main.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/main.py) — FastAPI App Factory
**Who calls it**: `uvicorn` starts this file.

Registers all routers under `/api/v1`:

| Router File | Prefix | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| [routes/resume.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/resume.py) | `/api/v1` | Upload resumes, trigger background parsing |
| [routes/github_routes.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/github_routes.py) | `/api/v1` | Trigger GitHub verification |
| [routes/unified_verification_routes.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/unified_verification_routes.py) | `/api/v1` | Run full unified verification |
| [routes/linkedin.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/linkedin.py) | `/api/v1` | LinkedIn scraping endpoint |
| [routes/verification.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/verification.py) | `/api/v1` | LinkedIn entity verification |
| [routes/search_routes.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/search_routes.py) | *(root)* | Web search endpoint |
| [routes/job_routes.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/job_routes.py) | `/api` | Job description endpoints |

> The routes are **thin controllers** — they validate inputs and immediately delegate to services. No ML logic lives in routes.

### [server.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/server.py) — Legacy Monolithic Server
An older, single-file server that duplicates some functionality. Contains its own resume parsing logic using [langextract](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/server.py#205-215). Still functional but the `app/` structure is the canonical, production path.

---

## 4. Orchestration: Two-Layer Architecture

> [!NOTE]
> There is no external orchestration framework. Two Python classes act as orchestrators using `asyncio`.

### Layer 1 — Top-Level Orchestrator: [unified_verification.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/unified_verification.py)

**Class**: [UnifiedVerificationService](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/unified_verification.py#68-465)  
**Singleton export**: `unified_verification_service`  
**Called by**: [routes/unified_verification_routes.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/routes/unified_verification_routes.py)

This is the **master controller**. It fires all three verification sources **concurrently** using `asyncio.gather()`:

```
UnifiedVerificationService.run_unified_verification()
        │
        ├── asyncio.gather(
        │       _verify_github(candidate_id, username, parsed_resume)
        │       _verify_linkedin(candidate_id, linkedin_url)
        │       _verify_web_search(candidate_id, profile_data)
        │   )
        │
        ├── _build_and_persist(candidate_id)
        │       └── _calculate_match_scores(github, linkedin, web)
        │
        └── _persist_to_db(verification_data)  → MongoDB
```

It also manages a **[VerificationCache](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/unified_verification.py#33-66)** (in-memory dict) to temporarily store intermediate results from each concurrent branch before merging them into a final `VerificationDataModel`.

---

### Layer 2 — GitHub Orchestrator: [github_services_v2/github_service.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/github_service.py)

**Public function**: [verify_github(candidate_id, parsed_resume)](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/github_service.py#48-82)  
**Called by**: `UnifiedVerificationService._verify_github()`

This runs a **sequential 15-step async pipeline**. The pipeline is failure-resilient — if any step throws, it is logged and execution continues with available data.

```
verify_github()
    └── _run_pipeline()
            Step 1:  Extract GitHub username from resume
            Step 2:  Fetch all public repos (github_client.py)
            Step 3:  Compute repo authenticity stats (_compute_repo_stats)
            Step 4:  Calculate RepositoryAuthenticity score
            Step 5:  Match resume projects → GitHub repos (project_matcher.py)
            Step 6:  Select top repos for deep analysis (_select_deep_repos)
            Step 7:  Fetch file trees for selected repos (github_client.py)
            Step 8:  Run code clone detection (code_similarity.py / CodeBERT)
            Step 9:  Run README plagiarism detection (readme_similarity.py)
            Step 10: Run behavioral/commit analysis (behavioral_analysis.py)
            Step 11: [LLM Escalation if needed] (llm_provider.py)
            Step 12: Fuse all signals into final score (signal_fusion.py)
            Step 13: Generate red flags (signal_fusion.py)
            Step 14: Build GitHubVerificationResult
            Step 15: Persist to MongoDB (github_writer.py)
```

---

## 5. ML Models & Algorithms

### 5.1 Resume Parsing — Gemini 2.5 Flash
**File**: [services/parser.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/parser.py)  
**How**: Sends resume text to Gemini via [langextract](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/server.py#205-215) + direct API. Extracts structured fields: name, email, skills, experience, education, projects, certifications, achievements.

### 5.2 Project ↔ Repo Matching — 3-Stage Hierarchy
**File**: [github_services_v2/matching/project_matcher.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/matching/project_matcher.py)  
**Model**: `BAAI/bge-large-en` (1024-dim embeddings, lazy-loaded, CPU-only)

Uses a 3-stage waterfall — faster stages run first, embedding only when needed:

| Stage | Method | Threshold |
|---|---|---|
| **Stage 1** | Exact normalised string match | exact |
| **Stage 2** | Fuzzy match via `rapidfuzz.token_set_ratio` | ≥ 85 |
| **Stage 3** | BGE-large embedding cosine similarity | configurable |

### 5.3 Code Clone Detection — CodeBERT
**File**: [github_services_v2/analysis/code_similarity.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/analysis/code_similarity.py)  
**Model**: `microsoft/codebert-base` (lazy-loaded, double-check locking)

Pipeline:
1. Fetch file tree from GitHub Trees API
2. Filter by language extension, enforce size limits
3. Normalise code (strip comments, licenses, trailing whitespace)
4. Chunk code into segments
5. Embed chunks with CodeBERT
6. Compute cosine similarity between candidate repo and reference repos
7. **If similarity is in the "suspicious" zone** (0.75–0.90): escalate to LLM

Has an **LRU + disk embedding cache** (SHA256 key) to avoid re-embedding known code.

### 5.4 LLM Escalation — Gemini → Groq Fallback
**File**: [github_services_v2/llm/llm_provider.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/llm/llm_provider.py)

Only invoked for **borderline plagiarism cases** (code similarity between `CODE_SIMILARITY_SUSPICIOUS` and `CODE_SIMILARITY_COPIED` thresholds).

```
escalate_to_llm()
    └── _call_llm()
            ├── Try: _call_gemini()  [gemini-2.0-flash via httpx REST]
            │       Returns: { verdict, reasoning, confidence }
            └── Fallback: _call_groq()  [Groq OpenAI-compatible API]
                    Returns: { verdict, reasoning, confidence }
```

- Temperature = 0.0 (deterministic)
- Hard timeout: 15 seconds
- Returns structured JSON verdict: `ORIGINAL | SUSPICIOUS | COPIED`

### 5.5 Signal Fusion Scoring — Weighted Average
**File**: [github_services_v2/scoring/signal_fusion.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/scoring/signal_fusion.py)

Combines all collected signals into a final authenticity score:

```
score = Σ(weight_i × signal_i)   for all available signals
score100 = score × 100
score40  = score100 × 0.4         (contribution to overall 40-point scale)
```

Signals include: `RepositoryAuthenticity`, `ResumeConsistency`, `CodeOriginality`, `ReadmeOriginality`, `BehavioralConsistency`.

If a signal is unavailable, its weight is **dynamically redistributed** proportionally among the remaining signals.

**Confidence** is computed from the standard deviation of available signal values:
- std < 0.15 → `HIGH`
- std ≤ 0.30 → `MEDIUM`
- std > 0.30 or < 3 signals → `LOW`

**Red flags** are rule-based (deterministic), NOT LLM-generated.

### 5.6 General Embeddings — all-MiniLM-L6-v2
**File**: [services/embedding_service.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/embedding_service.py)  
**Library**: `fastembed`  
**Dimensions**: 384

Used for general text similarity (e.g., job description matching). Lazy-loaded singleton, ~80MB download on first use.

### 5.7 LinkedIn/Web Entity Verification
**File**: [services/verifier.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/verifier.py)

- Generates name variations (abbreviations, permutations) for companies and universities
- Performs web search via [services/search.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/search.py)
- Scores results with `rapidfuzz` fuzzy matching + domain similarity
- Returns a confidence score per entity

