## 8. Key Design Decisions

### No External Agent Framework
Orchestration is done entirely with `asyncio` — no dependency on LangChain, LangGraph, or similar. This gives full control over timeouts, retries, and error handling and avoids framework version lock-in.

### LLM is a Last Resort
Gemini is only called in two scenarios:
1. Resume text parsing (always needed)
2. Code plagiarism — **only** when similarity falls in the ambiguous 0.75–0.90 range

This keeps API costs low and makes the system predictable.

### Failure Resilience
The GitHub 15-step pipeline uses try/except around each step. A failure in one step (e.g., CodeBERT times out) does NOT abort the pipeline — the result is computed with available signals via dynamic weight redistribution in [signal_fusion.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/scoring/signal_fusion.py).

### Lazy Model Loading
All ML models (CodeBERT, BGE-large, MiniLM) are **lazy-loaded on first use** with `asyncio.Lock()` double-check locking to prevent race conditions when multiple requests arrive simultaneously. Models are singletons held in module-level globals.

### Embedding Caching
CodeBERT embeddings are cached in a **LRU in-memory cache + optional disk cache** keyed by `SHA256(code_text)`. This avoids re-embedding the same code files across repeated verification requests.

### Dynamic Scoring
Signal weights are not fixed when signals are missing. [signal_fusion.py](file:///e:/beproject/ResumeAI-1/backend/app/services/github_services_v2/scoring/signal_fusion.py) redistributes the missing signal's weight proportionally across remaining signals, so a partial verification (e.g., no README available) still produces a meaningful score.
